  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM 2023 Flash Appeal for Fire Response in Camp 11</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 5 March 2023, a massive fire broke out in Block D of Camp 11 and quickly spread to adjacent camps, all sheltering Rohingya refugees in the Kutupalong-Balukhali area of Cox&#x2019;s Bazar district in Bangladesh. The affected areas are all under the International Organization of Migration (IOM)&#x2019;s Area of Responsibility. The fire consumed the shelters and personal belongings of thousands of Rohingya refugee families and essential facilities in the camps, leaving them temporarily displaced. Though no deaths have been reported, the incident caused significant damage to essential services and facilities and, thus, requires IOM to scale up its existing multi-sectoral response.Through this project, IOM is mitigating the impact of the fires on 15,926 Rohingya refugees and host community members through the provision of essential facilities and lifesaving aid in the sectors of Health, Protection, Site Management and Site Development, Shelter and Non-Food Items, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
